// Snippet: Variables
// Pattern: grog shop transaction — price rises each round (running gag)
// Features: <<declare>>, <<set>>, arithmetic expressions, {$variable} interpolation,
//            <<if>> / <<else>> conditionals driven by variable state
// Run: cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/snippets/variables.bub

title: Start
---
<<declare $doubloons = 12>>
<<declare $grogs_bought = 0>>
<<declare $price = 3>>

GrogVendor: Welcome to Griselda's Grog Shack. Finest grog in Barnacle Bay.
GrogVendor: Today's price is {$price} doubloons a mug. Supply and demand, as they say.

-> Buy a mug. <<if $doubloons >= $price>>
    <<set $doubloons = $doubloons - $price>>
    <<set $grogs_bought = $grogs_bought + 1>>
    <<set $price = $price + 2>>
    GrogVendor: Pleasure! That'll be {$price} for the next one. Inflation, ye understand.
    You: I have {$doubloons} doubloons left and {$grogs_bought} mug(s) in hand.
    <<jump Start>>
-> Ask about the price hike.
    GrogVendor: Each mug sold creates demand. It's economics!
    GrogVendor: Learned it from a travelling merchant. Suspicious fellow.
    <<jump Start>>
-> Leave.
    <<if $grogs_bought > 0>>
        GrogVendor: Come back when yer thirsty again. And richer.
        You: Spent {$doubloons} doubloons on {$grogs_bought} mug(s). Worth it.
    <<else>>
        GrogVendor: Not even one mug? Suit yerself.
    <<endif>>
===
